Building documents in the shell. str makes a string, obj a map from key and
document pairs, arr a list; push appends to a list, set puts a document at a
path (replacing what was there, or adding it, creating parents on the way);
concat joins two lists, join makes text from a list, split makes a list
from text, and collect makes a list from documents separated by a record
separator line. The calls keep results in registers and read them back
with the reader verbs, and end with the refusals each writer makes.
